milarity). Secreted by motor neuron and differentiated myotube cell lines, but not by undifferentiated myoblasts, possibly through the exosome pathway (PubMed:26503042)"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P41250"}],"value":"Cytoplasm","id":"SL-0086"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18614015"}],"value":"Mitochondrion","id":"SL-0173"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P41250"}],"value":"Cell projection, axon","id":"SL-0279"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26503042"}],"value":"Secreted","id":"SL-0243"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"26503042"}],"value":"Secreted, extracellular exosome","id":"SL-0466"}}]},{"commentType":"DISEASE","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16982418"}],"value":"Mice (Nmf249) heterozygous for the P278YK variant are used a model for human Charcot-Marie-Tooth 2D (CMT2D), which is caused by dominant GARS mutations. They exhibit reduced amplitudes of muscle compound action potentials and a large reduction in sciatic nerve conduction velocity in the absence of demyelination or remyelination, resulting from an age-related decrease in the number of large myelinated motor and sensory axons. The loss of myelinated axons is length-dependent, and there is a length- and time-dependent decrease in motor innervation of distal versus proximal muscles. Most of the axonal loss occurs by 1 month of age and mice that survive this period can be long-lived. At the molecular level, the P278YK mutation creates a neomorphic binding activity leading to the interaction of the variant with NRP1. This interaction competes out VEGFA binding and inhibits VEGFA-NRP1 signaling which is essential for motor neuron survival. VEGFA, but not GDNF treatment significantly ameliorates the loss of motor function in mutant mice"}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the class-II aminoacyl-tRNA synthetase family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Transit peptide","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":33,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Mitochondrion","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":34,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":729,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Glycine--tRNA ligase","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}],"featureId":"PRO_0000072999"},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":53,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":109,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"WHEP-TRS","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"PROSITE-ProRule","id":"PRU00531"}]},{"type":"Binding site","location":{"start":{"value":289,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":289,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","featureCrossReferences":[{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:57305"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P41250"}],"ligand":{"name":"glycine","id":"ChEBI:CHEBI:57305"}},{"type":"Binding site","location":{"start":{"value":321,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":323,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","featureCrossReferences":[{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P41250"}],"ligand":{"name":"ATP","id":"ChEBI:CHEBI:30616"}},{"type":"Binding site","location":{"start":{"value":332,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":333,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","featureCrossReferences":[{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P41250"}],"ligand":{"name":"ATP","id":"ChEBI:CHEBI:30616"}},{"type":"Binding site","location":{"start":{"value":340,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":340,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","feature